@page "/"

<PageTitle>StoryBuilder · Workshop</PageTitle>

<section class="page-head">
    <div class="eyebrow">The Singularity Workshop · StoryBuilder</div>
    <h1>Every universe starts somewhere.</h1>
    <p class="lede">A world can be larger than any book can list. Start with the person who opens the door, the event someone remembers, or the moment a campaign takes an unexpected turn. The archive grows as the story needs it.</p>
</section>

<div class="workbench-grid">
    <a class="panel stack" href="/casting">
        <div class="eyebrow">Door 01</div>
        <h2>Casting</h2>
        <p>Create a character without filling out a dissertation. Choose a starting pattern, add a phrase or a few traits, and revise them whenever the character changes.</p>
        <span>Enter the casting room →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="panel stack" href="/stage">
        <div class="eyebrow">Door 02</div>
        <h2>The Stage</h2>
        <p>Capture a fight or conversation as ordered actions, reactions, dialogue, and poses. Turn the beats into an editable narration draft.</p>
        <span>Build a scene →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="panel stack" href="/archive">
        <div class="eyebrow">Door 03</div>
        <h2>World Archive</h2>
        <p>Record historical claims and their sources. Keep what happened, what survived, and what people believe happened distinct.</p>
        <span>Open the archive →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="panel stack" href="/campaigns">
        <div class="eyebrow">Door 04</div>
        <h2>Campaign Room</h2>
        <p>Capture participant choices without predetermining the outcome. Proposed actions stay proposals until an author or table accepts them.</p>
        <span>Enter a campaign →</span>
    </a>
</div>

<section class="panel" style="margin-top:1rem">
    <div class="eyebrow">Design principle</div>
    <h2>Useful before complete.</h2>
    <p>Defaults reduce friction. Synonyms help you find language. Attribution preserves perspective. Nothing here requires you to enumerate every world or explain every character before you can begin.</p>
    <p class="muted">This is a local in-memory proof of the StoryBuilder domain and MicroBundle boundary. Refreshing the browser starts a new workspace; persistence and WebPage host integration are future steps.</p>
</section>
